    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the sum of the roots of the equation \\((x - 5)^2 = 9\\), we start by solving the equation. We take the square root of both sides:\n\n\\[\n\\sqrt{(x - 5)^2} = \\pm \\sqrt{9}\n\\]\n\nThis gives us two linear equations:\n\n\\[\nx - 5 = 3 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad x - 5 = -3\n\\]\n\nSolving these equations for \\(x\\), we get:\n\n\\[\nx = 5 + 3 = 8 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad x = 5 - 3 = 2\n\\]\n\nSo, the roots of the equation are \\(x = 8\\) and \\(x = 2\\). To find the sum of these roots, we add them together:\n\n\\[\n8 + 2 = 10\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the sum of the roots is \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{10}\n\\]",
